1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.801
Congratulations on completing the course.

2
00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.170
We hope that getting hands-on and building

3
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.473
A2A agents has sparked your creativity

4
00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:09.976
and got you excited about what's possible when agents collaborate effectively.

5
00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.979
Throughout this course, you've explored why A2A is valuable,

6
00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.181
learned its core principles, and actually built

7
00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.784
and ran your own A2A agents.

8
00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:22.489
The Agent2Agent protocol signals the maturation of the generative AI industry,

9
00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.691
the end of the wild west of isolated

10
00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:27.193
bots and the beginning of the internet of agents.

11
00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.929
By providing a rigorous, standardized, and

12
00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:32.799
secure method for autonomous systems to collaborate,

13
00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:37.470
A2A enables complex, multi-vendor workflows that were previously impossible.

14
00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:41.808
You can find sample code in the a2a-samples GitHub repo,

15
00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:46.513
and explore all the repositories in the google-a2a GitHub organization.

16
00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:50.517
All official A2A code will be added to repos in this organization.

17
00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.987
A2A is community governed and open,

18
00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.489
built by the community for the community.

19
00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.192
Whether you're building, contributing, or just curious,

20
00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.294
there's a place for you in this ecosystem.

21
00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.296
Please submit pull requests if you'd

22
00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.165
like to suggest improvements to the protocol

23
00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:06.966
or share your implementations.

24
00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.835
Thank you so much for learning with

25
00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.470
us and we can't wait to see

26
00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.939
what you create in the multi-agent world using A2A.
